Feature: slice-6 / error-code-translation-map
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-6
Verified: 2026-05-28

What was built
==============
A central translateError helper at src/lib/errors/translate.ts plus
the `errors` i18n namespace in PL + EN. Six admin catch-blocks that
previously surfaced raw `e.message` ("rpc error: code = PermissionDenied
desc = reason must be >= 10 characters") now route through this helper
and show a localized, human-friendly string.

Mapping order (first match wins):
  1. ConnectError message contains a known backend substring →
     errors.backend.<key>. Today: reasonTooShort, invitationExpired,
     invitationAccepted, quotaExceeded, subscriptionPastDue,
     alreadyExists.
  2. ConnectError.code → errors.code.<name>. All 16 Connect codes
     are wired (canceled, unknown, invalidArgument, deadlineExceeded,
     notFound, alreadyExists, permissionDenied, resourceExhausted,
     failedPrecondition, aborted, outOfRange, unimplemented,
     internal, unavailable, dataLoss, unauthenticated).
  3. Plain Error.message also runs through the backend-substring
     scan so non-Connect errors (e.g. Firebase Auth wrapped as
     Error) still get specific handling when a pattern matches.
  4. Otherwise → errors.generic.

A `tryT` fallback returns the bare key string if the i18n key is
missing — keeps dev-time additions from rendering MissingTranslation
exceptions that nuke the dialog.

Where it's wired
================
All 6 catch sites in:
  marketing-site/src/components/admin/OrgDetail.tsx  (4 actions:
    setStatus, resetTokens, changePlan, edit-org)
  marketing-site/src/components/admin/UsersList.tsx  (2 actions:
    UserEditDialog onConfirm, UserDeleteDialog onConfirm)

Each component pulls `const tErrors = useTranslations("errors")` and
calls `translateError(e, tErrors)` instead of stringifying e.message.

Not wired here (out of scope for this feature)
==============================================
- src/components/register/AcceptInviteForm.tsx already had bespoke
  ConnectError→message handling pre-Slice-6 (invalid/expired
  invitation). That code-path stays as-is; both routes now produce
  comparable copy, and the bespoke handler emits more nuanced text
  for the invite-specific failure modes. A follow-up can migrate it
  to translateError if/when the bespoke logic moves into the
  BACKEND_PATTERNS table.
- Firebase Auth errors (`auth/email-already-in-use` etc.) on the
  registration forms — those carry locale-specific UX copy already
  in `register.errors.*` and don't need re-routing.

